    "body": {
      "summary": "Tariff tables live in a shared drive as 40 CSV files. Load them into the warehouse as dbt seeds so billing models can join them and the data is reviewed in git.",
      "context": "- Repo: `acme-energy-dbt`, seeds go to `seeds/tariffs/`.\n- Related: DEMO-0040 (epic), DEMO-0041 (reconciliation tests need these seeds).\n- The monthly CSV export is produced by finance on the 1st; the tariff API lags by one day.",
      "requirements": "- All 40 tariff tables are loaded with explicit column types.\n- Seeds are refreshable with a single documented command.\n- `fct_billing` joins the seeds, tests cover tariff changes inside a month.",
      "out_of_scope": "- Live tariff API ingestion.\n- Historic tariffs before 2022.",
      "plan": "1. Export the CSVs (T1).\n2. Add `seeds/tariffs/schema.yml` with column types (T2).\n3. Join in `fct_billing` and add tests (T3).\n4. Document `make refresh-tariffs` in the README (T4).\n\nT2 and T3 run in parallel as subagent leases.",
      "decisions": "- **Chosen:** monthly CSV is the source of truth (Q1, Mara).\n- **Rejected:** API as source, because it lags one day and costs +1 day of work.",
      "verification": "- `dbt seed --select tariffs` exits 0 and loads 40 tables.\n- `dbt test --select fct_billing` passes.",
      "current_state": "T1 done, 40 CSVs exported. T2 (seed configs) and T3 (fct_billing join) are leased to two subagents. Both are blocked on Q2: DATE or TIMESTAMP for `valid_from`. T4 waits for Mara."
    },
